    "issued": "2026-01-01",
    "note": "Transcribed by hand from the federal directory of the cantonal AOCs (art. 25 of the Wine Ordinance, RS 916.140): each AOC as it writes it, the canton it is listed under, and its column — cantonal, regional or local. Its 63 AOCs: Vully, listed under Fribourg and Vaud, and Zürichsee, under Schwyz and Zürich, are intercantonal and counted once, as the directory says; neither is nested in a canton's AOC. A regional or local AOC lies within its canton's cantonal one, as the directory groups them; which regional AOC a local one lies in, it does not say. The directory lists Basel-Stadt under the abbreviation BL, read as BS. Only its facts are taken: names, cantons and kinds. A cantonal AOC is placed at its canton; a regional or local one at the place its name is, where OpenStreetMap has it, and otherwise at its canton's AOC, approximately. Lavaux and La Côte stand at Vaud's AOC: OpenStreetMap's places of those names in Vaud are elsewhere. Jura takes no article: \"Jura wine\" is France's. Six AOCs take an article of their own, found on the French and German Wikipedias: Lavaux, the Chablais (\"Chablais vaudois\", one of Vaud's six wine regions), Dézaley (\"Dézaley grand cru\"), Vaud and Valais (their vineyards' articles) and Zürichsee (\"Weinbau am Zürichsee\")."
